  "verbalization": "Dianversicoside G appears to have a shared target relationship with M19-MEL through a chain of interactions involving hepatocytes and other molecules. The evidence suggests that Dianversicoside G directly targets hepatocytes, which in turn are targets of terbutaline, a molecule that itself targets M19-MEL. Similarly, Dianversicoside G also targets Raji cells, which are targets of terbutaline and ultimately M19-MEL. This indicates a potential role for terbutaline as a bridge between Dianversicoside G and M19-MEL, possibly through a common pathway involving hepatocyte-mediated signaling. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, suggesting a robust connection, though the exact mechanism of action remains partially inferred. The relationship is supported by the presence of a common target in the chain, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between Dianversicoside G and M19-MEL.",
